how can i spark myself and my business  up it's a question I came in from one of  my newsletter readers Susie Susie Thanks  for writing in she basically wrote in to  say she's been running this business she  said I feel I used to be on fire about  my business but I've gradually sunk into  a certain amount of apathy and blind  averageness so I want to learn how to  spark both my business and myself up  again Susie first of all I want you to  know that this is very common this isn't  something that a lot of entrepreneurs  talk about nobody really told me about  this but it's very common if you've had  a business for a while it's really  common to lose touch with it to lose the  passion to lose the excitement you need  to always be putting something new into  the company to stay motivated to see  excited what I found to be the best  result for me is to try to tie my  personal interest as much as possible  into the business so when I first  started this business it was all about  the famous entrepreneur stories because  that's how I learned I learned through  the success of other famous  entrepreneurs applied their strategies  to make it work for me and my whole  website was basically just me sharing  stories of famous entrepreneurs it  wasn't even about me I wasn't on there  was just writing and learning from these  successful entrepreneurs and it involved  I started to get other people to write  content for me I stopped loving the  writing you didn't want to write anymore  and that could have been the end of my  business I could have said you know this  this this sucks i don't i don't want to  do this anymore I'm bored I'm tired I'm  not motivate anymore so i had to find  something different so then i became  interested in getting other people to  write for me and I went out and I  recruited almost 8,000 people to write  from my website from business coaches  marketing consultants up to Donald Trump  and that was exciting for a while and  then that became born you know jump was  my big fish I wanted to go and get him  and I was really excited and the ones we  landed him people just arted to come on  their own because we had so much  momentum and I need to find another  thing to get me going and that could  have been the end of my business there  too right the next thing I started do  responding people on newsletters so it  created my newsletter people started  running in with questions and then I  quickly got bombarded again with with  questions and I was writing again and  and it was great for a while but then it  became too much and overwhelming and I  lost the passion for doing that so I  said with the videos and now I'm doing  the videos and I loved in the videos and  and so far so good I still love doing  the videos but if I lose interest in the  videos then I'll move on to do something  else and I keep trying to bring what I  believe in what I'm excited passion  about into my business the whole core of  everything i do is still about believing  in entrepreneurs and so wherever that  takes me I'm always growing my business  in different directions and the projects  that have worked out I either continue  by having somebody on my team do or by  by dropping and I move on to something  else you need to find what you are  strongly and deeply passionate about  personally and then bring that into your  business more and that may change and  evolve and then your business evolves  with it the more of a personal  connection you bring to your company the  more fun you're going to have the more  you're going to attract ideal customers  the more passion I'm gonna bring your  company the more money you're going to  make I got into salsa I make that part  of my business I talk about salsa  anything that you're interested in bring  it into your company and see how it  flies come up with the one thing that  you staying for for me it's believed I  see it in them in a lot of my videos  it's an uplifting message is something  that I strongly am and proud of its part  of me and whatever business I went into  it would still be about belief if I was  selling shoes it be about believe with  shoes without selling apartments would  be about believe with apartments and I  love helping entrepreneurs so everything  that I do and everybody on my team they  believe in believe and they believe in  entrepreneurs and we build out from  there so you've got to find the one  thing that is core to you not to your  business but to you and then bring that  into everything that you do  I know it can be hard especially if  you've done the same thing for years and  years and years and it gets frustrating  and you don't know how to break the  cycle and it's a habit now it's a habit  that you wake up every day and you're  not excited about what you're doing give  yourself some time to think free up your  schedule a little bit to focus on  something new that you can do even if  it's not related to your business  because you can find a way to bring it  in a quick example I am an investor in  the salsa dancing company I talked a  little bit about it when I first joined  salsa it wasn't to try to find my next  big opportunity if you're always looking  for the next big thing then you're  rarely going to find it because you're  forcing it you've got to let it come to  you I started salsa dancing if I looked  at as a business opportunity it wouldn't  have made any sense and I woulda quit it  because I was learning too late my steps  were ginormous I didn't understand the  music I couldn't commit to doing this on  a full-time basis there were so many  strikes against me didn't make sense why  would I get into salsa and had no  background in this and I would have quit  if I was just looking as a business  opportunity but I started doing it just  out of the the desire to explore to  learn more about myself and do something  different and I loved it and I fell in  love and now I'm an investor in the  business I'll teach some classes I'll DJ  three times a week at our events I love  doing it it's part of me now it became a  business opportunity because I wasn't  out there trying to ram every thought I  had into creating this new idea so  homework for you and everybody watching  number one is fine what score to you  find the one word the one thought the  one belief that means something to you  that that you read it and it gets you  excited one word and then try to bring  that into everything that you're doing  and number two if you're looking for new  opportunities you looking for something  different give yourself the time the  freedom the flexibility to go out and  try new things without having the  pressure of it having to be the next big  thing  if you do that success will be yours and  if you have any problems in this if you  want to help brainstorm this you you  want to share your philosophy with me on  your business I will help guide you  through the process because I want to  see you become successful believe those  you watching you like the video you know  the drill thumbs up below please and I  want to hear you have to think leave a  comment underneath let me know what you  think you have a question for your  business let me know below you want a  brainstorm with me put your thoughts  down below and i'll make a video  response thank you so much and I'll see  you soon
 

